# Cloudflare Pages 301s for WordPress-only URL shapes that have no equivalent
# on the static rebuild. Top-level page slugs and /post/<slug>/ URLs were
# preserved 1:1, so they need no rules here (and adding any would risk loops).
#
# NOT handled here, by platform limitation: query-string URLs (?p=123,
# ?attachment_id=...) cannot be matched by _redirects. They need a Pages
# Function or Cloudflare Bulk Redirects at cutover. Attachment pages are also
# skipped: their WP shape (/<parent-slug>/<media-slug>/) is indistinguishable
# from real nested routes, so a wildcard would catch live pages.

# --- Feeds. The real feed now lives at /feed.xml (src/pages/feed.xml.ts). ---
# Splat rules also catch WordPress format variants (/feed/atom/, /feed/rss2/,
# /post/<slug>/feed/atom/, and so on). No built route contains a /feed segment,
# so the splats cannot shadow a real page.
/feed              /feed.xml      301
/feed/             /feed.xml      301
/feed/*            /feed.xml      301
/comments/feed     /feed.xml      301
/comments/feed/    /feed.xml      301
/comments/feed/*   /feed.xml      301
/post/:slug/feed   /post/:slug/   301
/post/:slug/feed/  /post/:slug/   301
/post/:slug/feed/* /post/:slug/   301
/category/:cat/feed   /category/:cat/   301
/category/:cat/feed/  /category/:cat/   301
/category/:cat/feed/* /category/:cat/   301

