# AMP retirement (GSC 404 sweep 2026-07-27).
# The old WordPress AMP plugin published TWO URL shapes, and Google still crawls
# both: "/<path>/amp/" (suffix) and "/amp/<path>/" (prefix, confirmed live on
# the homepage and /free-appraisal/). Every one of these has a live canonical
# page, so these are true 301s, not the soft-404 pattern we deliberately avoid
# for the query-string and /wp-content 404s.
#
# ORDER MATTERS, first match wins. The rule above for dating-a-les-paul stays
# ahead of everything here because that post has no live base page. The three
# guides below moved OUT of /post/ at cutover, so each needs an explicit rule
# ahead of the generic /post/:slug/amp rule; without it they would land on
# /post/<slug>/ and take a second hop.
/post/dating-a-les-paul-with-serial-numbers/amp                  /how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/   301
/post/dating-a-les-paul-with-serial-numbers/amp/                 /how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/   301
/post/how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/amp                      /how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/   301
/post/how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/amp/                     /how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/   301
